840404510498}}}, {"rawForm": "PolypGen dataset", "type": "dataset-name", "dataset-name": {"rawForm": "PolypGen dataset", "normalizedForm": "PolypGen dataset", "offsetStart": 170, "offsetEnd": 186, "boundingBoxes": [{"p": 13, "x": 229.924, "y": 114.764, "w": 67.41148749999999, "h": 8.637600000000006}]}, "normalizedForm": "PolypGen dataset", "context": "To provide generalisation capability of some state-of-the-art (SOTA) methods, we have used a set of popular and well-established semantic segmentation CNN models on our PolypGen dataset.", "mentionContextAttributes": {"used": {"value": true, "score": 0.7792898416519165}, "created": {"value": false, "score": 0.21979527175426483}, "shared": {"value": false, "score": 0.00091483851429075}}, "documentContextAttributes": {"used": {"value": true, "score": 0.7792898416519165}, "created": {"value": true, "score": 0.9986093640327454}, "shared": {"value": true, "score": 0.5122840404510498}}}, {"rawForm": "segmentation performances", "type": "dataset-implicit", "dataset-implicit": {"rawForm": "segmentation performances", "normalizedForm": "segmentation performances", "offsetStart": 47, "offsetEnd": 72, "bestDataType": "tabular data", "bestTypeScore": 0.9851, "hasDataset": 0.9998271465301514, "boundingBoxes": [{"p": 13, "x": 256.057, "y": 183.939, "w": 112.04479999999995, "h": 8.637599999999992}]}, "normalizedForm": "segmentation performances", "context": "We compute standard metrics used for assessing segmentation performances that includes Jaccard Index (JI =  T P  T P+FP+FN ), F1-score (aka Dice similarity coefficient, DSC), F2-score, precision (aka positive predictive value, PPV or p = T P T P+FP ), recall (r = T P T P+FN ), and overall accuracy (Acc.", "mentionContextAttributes": {"used": {"value": true, "score": 0.9979817867279053}, "created": {"value": false, "score": 0.0017692111432552338}, "shared": {"value": false, "score": 0.00024896266404539347}}}, {"rawForm": "Pyramid Scene Parsing Network (", "type": "dataset-name", "dataset-name": {"rawForm": "Pyramid Scene Parsing Network (", "normalizedForm": "Pyramid Scene Parsing Network (", "offsetStart": 0, "offsetEnd": 31, "boundingBoxes": [{"p": 13, "x": 56.693, "y": 697.824, "w": 143.15727500000003, "h": 8.63760000000002}]}, "normalizedForm": "Pyramid Scene Parsing Network (", "context": "Pyramid Scene Parsing Network (PSPNet) is designed to incorporate global context information for the task of scene parsing using context aggregation depending on different regions to take advantage of global context information.", "mentionContextAttributes": {"used": {"value": false, "score": 0.02273586206138134}, "created": {"value": true, "score": 0.9709559082984924}, "shared": {"value": false, "score": 0.006308328360319138}}, "documentContextAttributes": {"used": {"value": false, "score": 0.02273586206138134}, "created": {"value": true, "score": 0.9709559082984924}, "shared": {"value": false, "score": 0.006308328360319138}}}, {"rawForm": "PSPNet encoder", "type": "dataset-name", "dataset-name": {"rawForm": "PSPNet encoder", "normalizedForm": "PSPNet encoder", "offsetStart": 95, "offsetEnd": 109, "boundingBoxes": [{"p": 14, "x": 204.436, "y": 472.085, "w": 62.77508888888886, "h": 8.63760000000002}]}, "normalizedForm": "PSPNet encoder", "context": "The pyramid pooling module and CNN backbone with dilated convolutions are both present in the PSPNet encoder.. Similarly, dilated convolutions enabled the construction of semantic segmentation networks to effectively control the size of the receptive field that was incorporated in an a family of very effective semantic segmentation architectures, collectively named DeepLab .", "mentionContextAttributes": {"used": {"value": true, "score": 0.5982990264892578}, "created": {"value": false, "score": 0.3717045485973358}, "shared": {"value": false, "score": 0.029996376484632492}}, "documentContextAttributes": {"used": {"value": true, "score": 0.5982990264892578}, "created": {"value": false, "score": 0.3717045485973358}, "shared": {"value": false, "score": 0.029996376484632492}}}, {"rawForm": "DeepLabV", "type": "dataset-name", "dataset-name": {"rawForm": "DeepLabV", "normalizedForm": "DeepLabV", "offsetStart": 4, "offsetEnd": 12, "boundingBoxes": [{"p": 14, "x": 361.042, "y": 495.995, "w": 49.661, "h": 8.6376}]}, "normalizedForm": "DeepLabV", "context": "The DeepLabV3 capture multi-scale information by employing the atrous convolution at multiple rates in a cascade or parallel multi-scale context through spatial pyramid pooling.", "mentionContextAttributes": {"used": {"value": true, "score": 0.9423604607582092}, "created": {"value": false, "score": 0.055004917085170746}, "shared": {"value": false, "score": 0.0026346545200794935}}, "documentContextAttributes": {"used": {"value": true, "score": 0.9999898076057434}, "created": {"value": false, "score": 0.24289312958717346}, "shared": {"value": false, "score": 0.058072518557310104}}}, {"rawForm": "ResNet", "type": "dataset-name", "dataset-name": {"rawForm": "ResNet", "normalizedForm": "ResNet", "offsetStart": 56, "offsetEnd": 62, "boundingBoxes": [{"p": 14, "x": 298.491, "y": 519.906, "w": 29.9165, "h": 8.6376}]}, "normalizedForm": "ResNet", "context": "Moreover, ResUNet incorporates the benefits of both the ResNet and U-Net which allowed the design of a network with fewer parameters and improved segmentation performance.", "mentionContextAttributes": {"used": {"value": false, "score": 0.25604021549224854}, "created": {"value": true, "score": 0.7317792773246765}, "shared": {"value": false, "score": 0.012180465273559093}}, "documentContextAttributes": {"used": {"value": true, "score": 0.9999898076057434}, "created": {"value": true, "score": 0.7317792773246765}, "shared": {"value": false, "score": 0.058072518557310104}}}, {"rawForm": "DeepLabV", "type": "dataset-name", "dataset-name": {"rawForm": "DeepLabV", "normalizedForm": "DeepLabV", "offsetStart": 38, "offsetEnd": 46, "boundingBoxes": [{"p": 14, "x": 204.887, "y": 614.138, "